# W44-122 codec_wiki d=3 admit-DCT64 A/B — HONEST STOP

**Date**: 2026-05-20
**Workspace**: ~/work/zen/jxl-encoder--w44-122-codec-wiki-d3-dct64
**Harness**: jxl-encoder/examples/w44_122_ab.rs (clone of W44-104 retargeted)
**TSV**: w44_122_codec_wiki_d3_ab_2026-05-20.tsv
**Outcome**: HONEST-STOP — verifies the W44-104 ruling on a different cell;
W44-65 / W44-68 dct_suppress is load-bearing; admit-DCT64 here:
(a) doesn't reach the +2.0 SSIM2 acceptance gate on codec_wiki (max +1.40)
(b) regresses 11 OTHER screen cells by -0.37 to -1.44 SSIM2
(c) introduces +29% butteraugli regression on terminal e8/e9 (the W44-104
    regression cell from the very same suppression bypass)

## Background

W44-121 (`87466ec5`) dumped codec_wiki.png d=3 across e5/e6/e7 and found
the SAME ROOT-CAUSE PATTERN as W44-103/W44-104 on terminal d=4:
- DCT16X16 over-fires 100× vs cjxl (14031 vs 138 first-blocks)
- DCT64 family entirely absent from our output (vs cjxl 783-1019 fb)
- Per-region mean qac at PARITY (8.0-8.7 both sides)
- Cluster magnitude: -2.67 / -2.99 / -3.38 SSIM2 vs cjxl

W44-121 ranked "Candidate A: find_best_64x64_transform cost-model audit"
as highest EV (5-10 SSIM2 points expected). The dispatch task acknowledged
that W44-104 already RULED OUT the SAME LEVER on terminal d=4 but flagged
codec_wiki d=3 as potentially different regime (lower d, different mask
profile, post-W44-117/118/120 EPF improvements). This chunk performs the
direct A/B to test whether the lever transfers.

## Mechanism (confirmed identical to W44-104 finding)

W44-65 (`vardct/encoder.rs:2960-2963`) auto-fires
`dct_suppress = true` when `median(mask1x1) >= 99.5`. W44-68 extended
the suppression to also drop `try_dct32 = false` on the same class.

codec_wiki.png IS in the screenshot class (median ≈ 100.013 per
W44-65 promotion notes), so both flips fire by default. The DCT64
search is never run.

Smoke verified (e5/e6/e7 d=3 codec_wiki.png):
- AUTO (None)          : 79233 / 81576 / 68978 bytes  (W44-65 fires)
- FORCE-SUPPRESS (true): 79233 / 81576 / 68978 bytes  (byte-identical)
- ADMIT (false)        : 81303 / 84546 / 73021 bytes  (+2.6 / +3.6 / +5.9%)

