## Photo cells (regression probe)

24 photo cells (8 CID22 × e7 × d ∈ {1, 3, 5}) all show 0.000 byte
delta and 0.000 SSIM2 delta. **W44-65 does not fire on any tested
photo** (`median(mask1x1) < 99.5` per W44-65 promotion data: ≤92.34
for all 41 CID22 validation photos). The admit-hint has no effect on
photos — confirms the discriminator is correctly cutting at the
photo/screenshot boundary.

## Why admit is insufficient (root cause of partial close)

The W44-121 mechanism description matches the W44-104 finding:
cjxl's DCT64 picks on codec_wiki d=3 land predominantly on BLANK
background regions. Any transform reconstructs blank regions
perfectly. The SSIM2 loss is in TEXT regions where both encoders
(after admit) pick DCT8/DCT16-class. Admit recovers the blank-region
bytes savings (smaller per first-block) but doesn't fix the text
region quality.

This was the W44-104 falsified hypothesis: candidate A would close
the cluster. It does not — the cluster has TWO concurrent root
causes (W44-103/121 explicitly listed both): (1) strategy
distribution divergence (blank regions get DCT64 on cjxl, DCT16X16
on ours), AND (2) the text-region SSIM2 deficit that DCT64 doesn't
touch.

## Honest-stop decision

Per dispatch task decision tree:
> "If fix doesn't improve codec_wiki d=3: honest-stop. Pivot to
> W44-122 candidate B (DCT16X16 over-firing RC) or C (default-flip
> dct_suppress_hint)"

The fix DOES improve codec_wiki d=3 by +0.73 to +1.40 SSIM2, but
fails the +2.0 gate. Additionally it regresses 11 OTHER screenshot
cells (FIXED→OPEN) which violates the "zero new flips" gate. Pivot
to candidate B (DCT16X16 over-firing root-cause investigation) is
the right next chunk.

## Candidate C (default-flip dct_suppress_hint) is RULED OUT here

Per W44-104 explicit DO-NOT:
> "DO NOT default-flip `with_dct_suppress_hint` to `Some(false)`.
>  Measured cost: +4% bytes / ±0.3 SSIM2 on terminal, and the W44-62
>  data already showed all other gb82-sc screenshots ALSO benefit
>  from W44-65/W44-68 suppression"

This W44-122 measurement reconfirms: 11 screen cells regress under
admit. The W44-65 default is correctly protecting them.

## Recommended W44-123

Candidate B: DCT16X16 over-firing RC. Investigate why our
`find_best_32x32_transform` selects DCT16X16 100× more than cjxl on
screen-class regions. Per W44-121 top disagreement pair table:
DCT16X16 → DCT64X64 is the dominant divergence (28k cells at e5,
36k at e7). When W44-65 forces `try_dct64=false`, the split-vs-keep
decision at the 32×32 level should prefer DCT32X32 keep (4 blocks
covered) over four DCT16X16 first-blocks (8 sub-blocks). Currently
we pick DCT16X16. Possible culprits:
- `entropy_mul[DCT32X32]=1.21` may be too high relative to libjxl's
  effective value on screenshot suppression path
- `find_best_32x32_transform` may evaluate DCT32X32 with the wrong
  per-block-loss scaling when `mask1x1` is saturated
- The "DCT32X32 vs 4×DCT16X16" cost comparison may need a screenshot-
  class lift on DCT32X32

This is a NARROWER lever than candidate A (touches only
`find_best_32x32_transform` cost model, not the screenshot-suppress
gate), and per W44-121: "Expected EV: 2-5 SSIM2 points (subset of
Candidate A's gain — once DCT64 search wins, DCT16X16 over-firing
automatically resolves)" — but per this chunk's finding, DCT64
admission DOES NOT close the cluster, so DCT16X16-via-DCT32X32 may
be a complementary path that admits DCT32X32 without breaking
neighbors.

## Falsified hypotheses

| Hypothesis | Status | Evidence |
|---         |---     |---       |
| H1: codec_wiki d=3 admit closes the SSIM2 cluster (≥+2.0)   | FALSE | max +1.40 |
| H2: codec_wiki d=3 different regime from terminal d=4       | FALSE | same mechanism (W44-65 fires, admit produces ±0.3 SSIM2 noise on cluster, regresses neighbors) |
| H3: W44-117/118/120 EPF closure enables admit on screens    | FALSE | terminal e8/e9 butteraugli regresses +29% under admit |

